From: ares-7.3.3-port <no-reply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: mediatek,mtu3: add mediatek,mt6893-mtu3

MT6893 (Dimensity 1100) embeds a MediaTek USB3 DRD controller. The
ares board devicetree describes it with the two-string pair

    compatible = "mediatek,mt6893-mtu3", "mediatek,mtu3";

so that the mainline mtu3 driver (whose of_match contains the generic
"mediatek,mtu3" fallback) can bind without any driver-side change.
The schema's SoC-specific enum so far lists other MediaTek SoCs only,
so dtbs_check rejects the first string. Add it.

The node is converted to mainline form: clocks/clock-names use a single
clk26m fixed-clock with "sys_ck" (the driver uses
devm_clk_bulk_get_optional(), and the binding requires minItems: 1),
phys points at the generic-tphy-v2 u2port, dr_mode = "host", and the
4.14-private usb-role-switch / role-switch-default-mode are dropped.
No other schema change is needed.

Signed-off-by: ares-7.3.3-port <no-reply@localhost>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtu3.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtu3.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/mediatek,mtu3.yaml
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
     items:
       - enum:
           - mediatek,mt2712-mtu3
+          - mediatek,mt6893-mtu3
           - mediatek,mt8173-mtu3
           - mediatek,mt8183-mtu3
           - mediatek,mt8186-mtu3
